    fix(VERSION-002): seam test warms engine import - isolated runs failed (judge 8cb32a96)
    
    The Tier-2 judge (verdict 8cb32a96, criterion 2 FAIL) proved
    test_bridge_in_process_path_never_spawns_a_process passed only by
    import-caching accident: in the full file another test had already
    imported terminal_jail.interruptor, but in isolation the patched window
    covered the cold import, and decider.py computes _UNSHARE_PREFIX =
    unshare_prefix() at MODULE-IMPORT time (userns.py runs a real
    unshare ... true probe). The seam test now warms the engine import
    explicitly and its docstring documents why the one-time preflight is
    excluded from the no-spawn contract - it is production cost every real
    bridge process pays, not the per-assertion seam.
    
    Verified in all orders: isolated 1 passed; -k "never_spawns or
    real_exec_parity" 2 passed; full file 37 passed, 1 skipped; full plugin
    suite 1018 passed, 7 skipped; ruff clean.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
